           but plan_bridge never inserts an outcome and SQLite FKs are
           OFF by default -> the DDL integrity is not enforced at all
==============================================================================
  foreign_keys pragma default = 0
  sqlite version 3.40.1
  IntegrityError: CHECK constraint failed: typeof(pnl)='text'
  store construction path: does it enable foreign_keys?
apex/data_catalog/store/sqlite_store.py:8:synchronous=FULL, foreign_keys=ON, busy_timeout=5000), G16 (SQLite only —
apex/data_catalog/store/sqlite_store.py:348:        await self._db.execute("PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON;")
apex/research/checkpoints.py:120:        await self._db.execute("PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON")

DONE X-V7

==============================================================================
X-V7-005 CORRECTION: the store DOES enable foreign_keys=ON, so the FK IS
           enforced on the real path; my raw-connection claim was WRONG
==============================================================================
$ sed -n '340,352p' apex/data_catalog/store/sqlite_store.py
  348:        await self._db.execute("PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON;")
  8:  synchronous=FULL, foreign_keys=ON, busy_timeout=5000), G16 (SQLite only ...
  -> the connection factory enables it; a bare sqlite3.connect does not,
     which is why the probe above failed.  RETRACTED as a finding.
$ python3 -c "re-verify with the pragma ON"
  valid outcome insert OK
  FK enforced -> FOREIGN KEY constraint failed
  outcome DDL FK clause:
    ['FOREIGN KEY(setup_id) REFERENCES setup_candidate(setup_id)']
